Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:32:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Optional channel-chunked DINOv2 feature upsampling
 (--sem_dino_chunk)

Upsamples the 384-channel patch features in channel chunks and accumulates the dot
product and squared norms, instead of materializing full-resolution feature maps.
Default 0 keeps the previous computation unchanged; with chunking the similarity map
differs only at float32 rounding level (max ~1e-6, summation order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PHmjveU9kNqt1TKBUX99W4
---
 arguments/__init__.py |  1 +
 train_sim.py          |  2 +-
 utils/dino_utils.py   | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 utils/signal_maps.py  |  4 ++--
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arguments/__init__.py b/arguments/__init__.py
index f4d7a32..b0b01eb 100644
--- a/arguments/__init__.py
+++ b/arguments/__init__.py
@@ -111,6 +111,7 @@ class OptimizationParams(ParamGroup):
         self.sem_sample_ratio = 0.3       # rho of the stratified sampling
         self.sem_r9_threshold = 0.1       # r9 mode: error threshold
         self.sem_r9_cap = 0.05            # r9 mode: max fraction of Gaussians added per step
+        self.sem_dino_chunk = 0           # >0: upsample DINOv2 features in channel chunks of this size (less VRAM)
         self.sem_blur_sigma = 4.0         # l1_blur: Gaussian blur sigma (px)
         self.sem_shadow = "none"          # extra signal back-projected through the 3rd aux channel (logging only)
         self.sem_split = "adc"            # adc (densify_and_split_by_selected_mask) | mask2
diff --git a/train_sim.py b/train_sim.py
